Why This Happens
Immediate Synchronous Emission: from([1, 2, 3, 4, 5]) emits all five values synchronously one right after another at time $t = 0$.

Cancellation by switchMap: Every time switchMap receives a new value,
 it cancels/unsubscribes from the previous inner Observable and switches to the new one:
 Value 1 arrives -------> starts 1-second delay timer -------> immediately canceled when 2 arrives.
 Value 2 arrives -------> starts 1-second delay timer -------> immediately canceled when 3 arrives.
 Value 3 arrives -------> starts 1-second delay timer -------> immediately canceled when 4 arrives.
 Value 4 arrives -------> starts 1-second delay timer -------> immediately canceled when 5 arrives.
 Value 5 arrives -------> starts 1-second delay timer.
 Completion: Because no higher values arrive to cancel 5, its inner Observable finishes after the 1000 ms delay, executing the tap log and emitting 10 ($5 \times 2$).




 